 ],
 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "Your village needs a road, so you just drive on the dirt. Problem solved!",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But when the monsoon arrives, the dirt turns into deep mud.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you spread a layer of gravel. Now the wheels have something hard to grip.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But heavy trucks push the gravel down into the soft mud underneath.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you build a thick base of crushed rock, packed tight, and seal it with asphalt.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But rain sits in puddles, seeps into tiny cracks, and soaks the base.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Every truck pumps that wet base out, and the road breaks into potholes.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you make the middle a little higher, and the water runs off to the sides.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "And you dig ditches along both edges, to carry the water away from the base.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Congratulations! You just built a road. What should we build next?",
   "pausa": 0.2
  }
 ],
